<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Hokuzan</h1><p class="st-meta">1322 CE – 1416 CE (approx.) · capital Nakijin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The northern kingdom of 14th-century Okinawa, centred on the great stone castle of Nakijin, conquered by Chuzan in 1416.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hokuzan arose in the early 14th century in the mountainous north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okinawa-island">Okinawa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/motobu-peninsula">Motobu</a> peninsula, one of three rival kingdoms that formed as local lords consolidated power. Its seat was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakijin-castle">Nakijin</a>, whose long, winding stone walls survive as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hokuzan was the largest of the three kingdoms in area but the poorest in farmland. Its kings Haniji, Min and Hananchi sent tribute missions to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming China</a> from 1383, and the castle has yielded Chinese ceramics that show active trade. Power rested on alliances with local aji lords.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-hashi">Sho Hashi of Chuzan</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakijin-castle">Nakijin</a> in 1416 with the help of disaffected Hokuzan lords; King Hananchi killed himself. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chuzan">Chuzan</a> then appointed a warden to govern the north.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/hokuzan.jpg" alt="Hokuzan" width="320" height="405"><figcaption>Image: kallgan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ryukyu_Kingdoms_of_Sanzan_era.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1322 CE – 1416 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nakijin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Haniji, Min, Hananchi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ryukyuan religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Okinawan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sanhoku, Hokuzan Kingdom, Shanbei</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1369&amp;focus=hokuzan" aria-label="Hokuzan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8053 1198 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hokuzan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8373 1454L7643 1242M8373 1454L8372 1470"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7643 1242h0M8372 1470h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8373 1454h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8373 1454h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nakijin. <a href="/atlas?year=1369&amp;focus=hokuzan">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

